cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this research archive and identify the exact knowledge/publication edition used."
title: "HEAV3NS-BROCWIN: Browser-hosted execution and preservation research"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "HEAV3NS-BROCWIN contributors"
version: "1.4.1"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research archive for original legacy Windows MMO client execution through
  a synthetic browser-hosted compatibility runtime. Client acceptance remains
  blocked; no production readiness, 3x startup gain, or long-duration reliability
  is established. The declared project license covers eligible source and
  authored documentation, with third-party and original game/platform exclusions
  documented in LICENSES/README.md. Publication edition 1.0.1 is a separate
  documentary edition dated 2026-10-11.
keywords:
  - software preservation
  - WebAssembly
  - Windows compatibility
  - legacy software

repository-code: "https://github.com/CardSorting/BROCWIN"
url: "https://github.com/CardSorting/BROCWIN"
